Subject: [PATCH 29/37] feat: restore the real backtest loop, wired to the
 fixed pipeline

Replays generate_trading_signal + approve_trade + BacktestEngine.
execute_trade (which now itself correctly calls simulate_trade) candle
by candle after an indicator warmup period, so a backtest exercises
the exact same decision logic as main.py's live path. Previously
stopped after loading indicator data, since the pipeline it would have
called was non-functional (see Milestone 1/2b findings).

Raises MarketDataError if there isn't enough history to clear the
warmup period, rather than silently running with cold indicators.
run_backtest() now returns the BacktestEngine so callers can inspect
.statistics()/.trades/.equity_curve.

Verified end-to-end against SimulationGateway across 1000+ candles
with no crashes.
